(
========================================================================
 PUZZLESCRIPT MESSAGES & ADVANCED FLOW TUTORIAL
 Paste this whole file into the editor at puzzlescript.net and hit RUN.
 Written for classic PuzzleScript - not any of the community forks.
 Every command below was checked against increpare's own engine source
 and documentation, not guessed from memory.
========================================================================

 TUTORIAL MAP -- Ctrl+F for a tag like [T3] to jump straight to it.

 [T0]  Prelude / Objects / Legend / Sounds / CollisionLayers - skim it
 [T1]  Attached MESSAGE: shown the instant a level's win-condition fires
 [T2]  Standalone MESSAGE screens: interstitials with no map behind them,
       plus back-to-back MESSAGE lines queuing up as separate screens
 [T3]  The in-RULE "message" command: a mid-level popup that does NOT
       advance to the next level - different mechanism from [T1]/[T2]
 [T4]  CHECKPOINT: a rule-triggered save point
 [T5]  RESTART: a rule-triggered "press R" - and how [T4] quietly moves
       the spot RESTART (and the real R key) sends you back to
 [T6]  CANCEL: reverting an entire turn, not just blocking one cell
 [T7]  WIN: winning straight from a rule, no WINCONDITIONS geometry
       needed at all
 [T8]  noundo / norestart: taking the Z and R keys away from the player
       entirely - a Prelude-wide switch, not a per-level one
 [T9]  Combining a normal rewrite with a trailing command in one rule
 [T10] Grab bag: keybindings, debug/verbose_logging, message limits,
       and one real discrepancy between the docs and the engine

 Every tag above appears twice more below: once as a comment right
 above the RULES it describes (skipped by [T1]/[T2]/[T8], which are
 not RULES-section features at all), and once above the LEVEL that
 demonstrates it. Each level's own attached MESSAGE recaps the point.

 One structural fact worth knowing before you start: WINCONDITIONS is
 ONE block for the whole file, checked after every level, not per
 level. "Some Player on Exit" below applies to [T7]'s level too, even
 though that level has no Exit tile on it anywhere - see [T7] for why
 that matters.

 Want the fork-only extensions - in-game level-select menus, a pause
 menu, message alignment, chapter branching? Those aren't part of
 classic PuzzleScript and won't compile here. See the companion files
 puzzlescript_plus_messaging.pss and puzzlescript_next_messaging.pss
 in this same repo instead - each needs a different, fork-specific
 editor to run, as explained in its own header.
========================================================================
)

